Irene - is an adventurer's daughter; father likely told her how to act in such situation. 
"Hey, Irene! What did father tell you of where they were staying overnight here?"
"They tried to find a cave for rest here" she replied. "He said, it was dangerous to stay in the open. This place is teeming with predators, Henry!"
She shivered and seemed was about to cry.
"Henry, what are we going to do? The night is close, what will happen to us? We will be eaten."
"It's like you said, we'll find a cave. Everything is going to be fine."
You calm Irene down, but your own voice treacherously trembles. You have no idea where to look for a cave. And in general, maybe there are no caves in this part of the island.
But appears, that luck is on your side today. Close to a glade you find spacious and dry grotto, plus it was absolutely uninhabited for your general relief. Now you can try to prepare for the night. Or you should do something else first?